# {{NAME}} backlog

Snapshot: {{DATE}}. This file owns task status until an external tracker is explicitly adopted.

Use IDs {{PREFIX}}-001 onward. Priority: P1 next, P2 later, P3 optional. States:

- Draft: scope or acceptance needs definition.
- Ready: bounded and actionable; does not grant execution authorization.
- In progress: active work with an accountable owner.
- Blocked: name the actual dependency and how it can be resolved.
- Done: acceptance evidence is recorded.
- Dropped: retain the reason instead of silently deleting the item.

No product work is complete solely because these files exist. Populate the first few real items from confirmed context, including outcome, owner, dependencies and acceptance. Split larger tasks only when a separate result can be reviewed.
